feat(editor): embed Kinescope videos

A Kinescope link pasted into an Embed block, an Embed activity or a ```embed
fence is not recognised: the editor iframes the share page as-is, the AI tools
reject it, and a ```video fence with it gets no hint.

Add Kinescope to the embed providers in both twins, embedProviders.ts and
embeds.py: kinescope.io/<id> and /embed/<id> become
https://kinescope.io/embed/<id>, keeping player parameters (t, seek, duration).
The Embed activity frames it 16:9 like the other video hosts, the editor hint
lists it, and content_assets points a Kinescope page at an embed block.
lib/media/kinescope.ts (new) holds the URL rules.

Covered by `editor-blocks.test.mjs` and `embed-url.test.mjs` (share and embed
links, parameters kept, the HLS manifest left alone), `kinescope.test.mjs` (the
URL rules) and `test_block_specs.py` (every provider example becomes its
player, Kinescope edge cases).
